  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.4.32 (forks 2.4.31) - FIX (OpenCL, Wasm, WebGL; silent wrong results): float -> Half conversion rounds to fp16 (was the identity). FIX (OpenCL, WebGPU, WebGL; silent wrong results): fp32 division and square root are correctly rounded, as .NET computes them (OpenCL: -cl-fp32-correctly-rounded-divide-sqrt, AMD RX 590 and NVIDIA RTX 4070 both differed from .NET before; WebGPU / WebGL: integer-exact division and sqrt, D3D was up to 2.5 ulp off). FIX (WebGPU; silent wrong results): a kernel with irreducible control flow (a goto into a loop) lost the code after that region. FIX (Velocity): a switch leaving a loop threw. PERF (Wasm): functions without barriers use structured control flow (block / loop / if) instead of a br_table state machine: a 960-step branchy loop 25 -> 2.8 ns per step. PERF (Velocity host path, CPU accelerator): ArrayView accessors optimized from the first call (a 960-step loop 13 -> 3.9 ns per step; Codecs VP9 Velocity inter frame 787 -> 245 ms). New tests on every backend: StructuredControlFlow_*, BranchCost_*, FloatDivision_*. See CHANGELOG.md.",
